    <title>Dexterous In-Hand Manipulation from Monocular Human
  Demonstration</title>
    <summary>  We present a system that learns in-hand reorientation from single-camera
video of human hands. On a 16-DoF hand the policy reaches a 78% success rate
across 40 unseen objects, compared with 51% for the prior state of the art.
</summary>
